Subject: [PATCH 499/499] Model loading: --load-format direct, B12X's
 bounce-mode O_DIRECT loader in vLLM

The production recipe loads with B12X's checkpoint loader through its
b12x_loader plugin. This moves the path GB10 takes into the tree, so the
reads, copies and transforms stay the same and vLLM owns the code:

- direct_loader.DirectModelLoader (from b12x/integration/vllm/loader.py and
  the in-tree b12x_loader.py): meta tensors that carry checkpoint ranges,
  routed by the model's weight loaders through weight_transfer; tables the
  model routes as files (checkpoint_file_weight_filter, DS4.1's Engram)
  yielded as vLLM's file-source descriptors, merged by name, never read.
- direct_io/ (from b12x/loader at 236ddff04a5f): DirectWeightSession's bounce
  path and the C helper's direct, batch and bounce readers. io_uring
  O_DIRECT reads into a 16-slot ring of 1 MiB registered host slots, a
  copier thread's cudaMemcpy2DAsync into the destinations, BF16->FP32
  expanded in the slot, other dtype conversions through an 8 MiB GPU
  scratch. Nothing is memory-mapped or read through the page cache.

Dropped: GDS, the shared read group, the PLE reader, the IPC-exportable
allocations and the progress panel. The loader refuses a device without
host page tables instead of falling back to GDS, and logs one summary line
("Direct loader: weights loaded, ..."). liburing is now required to build
the helper, which is otherwise B12X's code: it builds at first use into
$XDG_CACHE_HOME/vllm/direct_io/<digest>. The descriptor planning is moved
into functions of its own (view_offset, view_records, scratch_chunks) so
it can be checked without a GPU. B12X is Apache-2.0; every ported file
names its source and what changed.

Tests without a GPU (test_direct_loader.py): descriptors for TP column
and row shards, padded and transposed destinations, expert slices, byte
casts, E8M0 views, scalars and BF16 expansion, executed on host memory
with _batch.c's semantics, equal Torch's copies; scratch reads cover a
conversion exactly; refused views; header checks, name/prefix/index/skip
selection and coalesced metadata reads with preads in place of the helper;
registration and options; the refusal without host page tables; Engram
file-backed descriptors beside routed weights in a mixed shard, a table-
only shard never opened, the index and the expert filter on both; the
helper built once into the XDG cache, and refused without liburing.

Tests on a GPU (test_direct_loader_cuda.py, under DIRECT_IO_TEST_DIR,
/cache/direct-io-test by default, since O_DIRECT needs a real filesystem):
B12X's test_direct.py for the bounce ring, the helper's capabilities, a
loader-routed module whose weight digest equals a Torch copy's, and file-
backed tables beside routed weights. Not run: no GPU during the freeze.
